@@ -0,0 +1,272 @@
+Feature: TodoMVC
+  As a user
+  I want to manage a todo list
+  So that I can track tasks I need to complete
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  # ── No todos ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+
+  Rule: Empty state
+
+  Scenario: Main and footer are hidden when there are no todos
+    Given there are no todos
+    Then "#main" is not visible
+    And "#footer" is not visible
+
+  # ── New todo ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+
+  Rule: Adding a new todo
+
+  Scenario: Enter a new todo
+    When I type "Buy milk" into ".new-todo"
+    And I press Enter
+    Then the todo list contains 1 item
+    And the new todo has title "Buy milk"
+    And the new todo is not completed
+    And ".new-todo" is cleared
+
+  Scenario: Trimming whitespace from input
+    When I type "   Walk the dog   " into ".new-todo"
+    And I press Enter
+    Then the todo list contains 1 item
+    And the new todo has title "Walk the dog"
+
+  Scenario: Empty input is ignored
+    When I type "   " into ".new-todo"
+    And I press Enter
+    Then the todo list is empty
+
+  # ── Mark all as complete ──────────────────────────────────────────
+
+  Rule: Toggle all todos
+
+  Scenario: Mark all as complete toggles every todo
+    Given the todo list has items:
+      | title       | completed |
+      | Task One    | false     |
+      | Task Two    | false     |
+      | Task Three  | false     |
+    When I click "#toggle-all"
+    Then all todos are completed
+    And "#toggle-all" is checked
+
+  Scenario: Mark all unchecks when one todo is unchecked
+    Given the todo list has items:
+      | title       | completed |
+      | Task One    | true      |
+      | Task Two    | true      |
+      | Task Three  | false     |
+    Then "#toggle-all" is not checked
+
+  Scenario: Mark all checks when all todos are completed
+    Given the todo list has items:
+      | title       | completed |
+      | Task One    | true      |
+      | Task Two    | true      |
+    Then "#toggle-all" is checked
+
+  # ── Item ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+
+  Rule: Todo item interactions
+
+  Scenario: Checking a todo marks it completed
+    Given the todo list has item "Buy milk"
+    When I click the toggle for "Buy milk"
+    Then the item "Buy milk" has class "completed"
+
+  Scenario: Unchecking a todo removes completed state
+    Given the todo list has item "Buy milk" completed
+    When I click the toggle for "Buy milk"
+    Then the item "Buy milk" does not have class "completed"
+
+  Scenario: Double-clicking a todo label enters edit mode
+    Given the todo list has item "Buy milk"
+    When I double-click the label for "Buy milk"
+    Then the item "Buy milk" has class "editing"
+
+  Scenario: The destroy button is present on todo items
+    Given the todo list has item "Buy milk"
+    Then the item "Buy milk" has a ".destroy" button
+
+  # ── Editing ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+
+  Rule: Editing a todo
+
+  Scenario: Saving edit on Enter
+    Given the todo list has item "Buy milk"
+    When I double-click the label for "Buy milk"
+    And I change the edit field to "Buy almond milk"
+    And I press Enter in the edit field
+    Then the item "Buy milk" is renamed to "Buy almond milk"
+    And the item "Buy milk" does not have class "editing"
+
+  Scenario: Saving edit on blur
+    Given the todo list has item "Buy milk"
+    When I double-click the label for "Buy milk"
+    And I change the edit field to "Buy oat milk"
+    And the edit field loses focus
+    Then the item "Buy milk" is renamed to "Buy oat milk"
+    And the item "Buy milk" does not have class "editing"
+
+  Scenario: Empty edit destroys the todo
+    Given the todo list has item "Buy milk"
+    When I double-click the label for "Buy milk"
+    And I change the edit field to ""
+    And I press Enter in the edit field
+    Then the todo list is empty
+
+  Scenario: Whitespace-only edit destroys the todo
+    Given the todo list has item "Buy milk"
+    When I double-click the label for "Buy milk"
+    And I change the edit field to "   "
+    And I press Enter in the edit field
+    Then the todo list is empty
+
+  Scenario: Escape discards edits
+    Given the todo list has item "Buy milk"
+    When I double-click the label for "Buy milk"
+    And I change the edit field to "Buy oat milk"
+    And I press Escape in the edit field
+    Then the item "Buy milk" has title "Buy milk"
+    And the item "Buy milk" does not have class "editing"
+
+  # ── Counter ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+
+  Rule: Active todo counter
+
+  Scenario: Counter shows number of active todos
+    Given the todo list has items:
+      | title       | completed |
+      | Task One    | false     |
+      | Task Two    | true      |
+      | Task Three  | false     |
+    Then ".todo-count" shows "2 items left"
+
+  Scenario: Counter uses singular "item" for 1
+    Given the todo list has items:
+      | title       | completed |
+      | Task One    | false     |
+      | Task Two    | true      |
+    Then ".todo-count" shows "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: Counter shows "0 items left" when all completed
+    Given the todo list has items:
+      | title       | completed |
+      | Task One    | true      |
+      | Task Two    | true      |
+    Then ".todo-count" shows "0 items left"
+
+  # ── Clear completed ───────────────────────────────────────────────
+
+  Rule: Clear completed button
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed removes completed todos
+    Given the todo list has items:
+      | title       | completed |
+      | Task One    | true      |
+      | Task Two    | false     |
+      | Task Three  | true      |
+    When I click ".clear-completed"
+    Then the todo list has 1 item
+    And the remaining todo has title "Task Two"
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed is hidden when no completed todos
+    Given the todo list has items:
+      | title       | completed |
+      | Task One    | false     |
+      | Task Two    | false     |
+    Then ".clear-completed" is not visible
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed is visible when there are completed todos
+    Given the todo list has items:
+      | title       | completed |
+      | Task One    | true      |
+      | Task Two    | false     |
+    Then ".clear-completed" is visible
+
+  # ── Persistence ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
+
+  Rule: localStorage persistence
+
+  Scenario: Todos survive page reload
+    Given the todo list has items:
+      | title       | completed |
+      | Task One    | false     |
+      | Task Two    | true      |
+    When the app is reloaded
+    Then the todo list has 2 items
+    And the item "Task One" is not completed
+    And the item "Task Two" is completed
+
+  Scenario: localStorage key is "todos-vanillajs"
+    Given the todo list has item "Test"
+    Then localStorage has a key "todos-vanillajs"
+
+  Scenario: Editing state is not persisted
+    Given the todo list has item "Buy milk"
+    When I double-click the label for "Buy milk"
+    And I change the edit field to "not saved"
+    When the app is reloaded
+    Then the item "Buy milk" has title "Buy milk"
+    And the item "Buy milk" does not have class "editing"
+
+  # ── Routing ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+
+  Rule: Routing and filtering
+
+  Scenario: Default route shows all todos
+    Given the todo list has items:
+      | title       | completed |
+      | Task One    | false     |
+      | Task Two    | true      |
+    When the route is "#/"
+    Then the todo list shows 2 items
+    And the "All" filter link has class "selected"
+
+  Scenario: Active route shows only active todos
+    Given the todo list has items:
+      | title       | completed |
+      | Task One    | false     |
+      | Task Two    | true      |
+      | Task Three  | false     |
+    When the route is "#/active"
+    Then the todo list shows 2 items
+    And the list includes "Task One"
+    And the list includes "Task Three"
+    And the list does not include "Task Two"
+    And the "Active" filter link has class "selected"
+
+  Scenario: Completed route shows only completed todos
+    Given the todo list has items:
+      | title       | completed |
+      | Task One    | false     |
+      | Task Two    | true      |
+      | Task Three  | false     |
+    When the route is "#/completed"
+    Then the todo list shows 1 item
+    And the list includes "Task Two"
+    And the list does not include "Task One"
+    And the "Completed" filter link has class "selected"
+
+  Scenario: Completing a todo hides it in active filter
+    Given the todo list has items:
+      | title       | completed |
+      | Task One    | false     |
+      | Task Two    | false     |
+    When the route is "#/active"
+    And I click the toggle for "Task One"
+    Then the todo list shows 1 item
+    And the list includes "Task Two"
+
+  Scenario: Active filter is persisted on reload
+    Given the todo list has item "Test"
+    When the route is "#/active"
+    And the app is reloaded
+    Then the "Active" filter link has class "selected"
+
+  Scenario: Clicking a filter link changes the route
+    Given the todo list has item "Test"
+    When I click the "Completed" filter link
+    Then the route is "#/completed"
\ No newline at end of file
